  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q11",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Show that $9^{n+1}-3^{2n-1}$ is a multiple of 13 for all positive integers $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$9^{n+1}-3^{2n-1}=26\\times3^{2n-1}=13(2\\times3^{2n-1})$. Since $2\\times3^{2n-1}$ is an integer, the expression is a multiple of 13.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}9^{n+1}-3^{2n-1}&=3^{2n+2}-3^{2n-1}\\\\&=3^{2n-1}(3^3-1)\\\\&=26\\times3^{2n-1}\\\\&=13(2\\times3^{2n-1})\\end{align*}$$\nFor every positive integer $n$, $2\\times3^{2n-1}$ is an integer. Therefore the expression is a multiple of 13.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
